@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: Project Details
	Testing the Project Details portlet.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                          |
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker with the role "Manager" to the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a project with the following values
	| Name                       | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code                       | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type                       | Group              |
	| Industry                   | Automotive         |
	| Partner Code               | Zen OSB Partner    |
	| Partner First Line Support | true               |
	| Tier                       | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts               | 10                 |
	| Address Line               | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country                    | United States      |
	| State                      | California         |
	| City                       | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip                        | 91765              |
	| Region                     | US                 |
	| Language                   | English            |
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Watcher" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	* I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	* I add an order with the product "Digital Enterprise Production" and support level "Platinum" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	* I add an order with the product "Liferay Commerce Connectors Production" and support level "Floating" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the partner workers with the following email addresses for the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENOSBA |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen OSB Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View project
	New projects created in OSB should be visible in the project details page.

	Given I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I go to the project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	Then the project details with the following values should be visible
	| Project Code    | ZENOSBA         |
	| Status          | APPROVED        |
	| Level           | Platinum        |
	| Support Region  | US              |
	| Partner         | Zen OSB Partner |
	| Partner Support | Yes             |
	| Tier            | Premier         |
	| Industry        | Automotive      |
	| Last Modified   | Today           |
	| Modified By     | Amos Fong       |
	When I go to the Team Members tab
	Then the team member with the name "OSB Customer1" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Customer1                       |
	| Role  | Developer                           |
	| Email | osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the team member with the name "OSB Customer2" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | OSB Customer2                       |
	| Role  | Watcher                             |
	| Email | osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I go to the Offerings tab
	Then the offering with the product name "Portal Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Portal Production |
	| SLA              | Gold              |
	| Start Date       | Today             |
	| Support End Date | 1 year from now   |
	| Licenses         | 0 / 10000         |
	| Tickets          | Unlimited         |
	| Version          | 6                 |
	| Instance Size    | Sizing 1          |
	| Status           | ACTIVE            |
	And the offering with the product name "Digital Enterprise Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Digital Enterprise Production |
	| SLA              | Platinum                      |
	| Start Date       | Today                         |
	| Support End Date | 1 year from now               |
	| Licenses         | 0 / 1                         |
	| Tickets          | Unlimited                     |
	| Version          | 7                             |
	| Instance Size    | Sizing 1                      |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                        |
	And the offering with the product name "Liferay Commerce Connectors Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Liferay Commerce Connectors Production |
	| SLA              | Floating                               |
	| Start Date       | Today                                  |
	| Support End Date | 1 year from now                        |
	| Licenses         | 0 / 0                                  |
	| Tickets          | 0                                      |
	| Instance Size    | Sizing 1                               |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                                 |
	When I go to the History tab
	Then the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Amos Fong         |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Customer |
	| Update Date                 | Today             |
	| Update Field Name           | Role              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A               |
	| Update Field New Value      | Developer         |
	And the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "User" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Amos Fong         |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Customer |
	| Update Date                 | Today             |
	| Update Field Name           | User              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A               |
	| Update Field New Value      | OSB Customer1     |
	And the history entry in position number "2" with the field value "Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Amos Fong         |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Customer |
	| Update Date                 | Today             |
	| Update Field Name           | Role              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A               |
	| Update Field New Value      | Watcher           |
	And the history entry in position number "2" with the field value "User" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Amos Fong         |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Customer |
	| Update Date                 | Today             |
	| Update Field Name           | User              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A               |
	| Update Field New Value      | OSB Customer2     |

Scenario: Add portal environment details
	Users should be able to add portal environment details via the Project Details page.

	Given I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I go to the project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I add an environment configuration with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment One |
	| Product            | Portal Production          |
	| Liferay Version    | 6.2 EE                     |
	| Operating System   | Windows Server 2012        |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 7               |
	| Application Server | Tomcat 7.0                 |
	| Database           | MariaDB 10.0               |
	| Cloud Services     | Azure SQL Databases        |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	| Portal EXT         | portal-ext.properties      |
	| Patch Info         | patchinfo.txt              |
	Then the environment configuration with the name "Zen Portal Environment One" should be visible with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment One |
	| Product            | Portal Production          |
	| Liferay Version    | 6.2 EE                     |
	| Operating System   | Windows Server 2012        |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 7               |
	| Application Server | Tomcat 7.0                 |
	| Database           | MariaDB 10.0               |
	| Cloud Services     | Azure SQL Databases        |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	| Portal EXT         | portal-ext.properties      |
	| Patch Info         | patchinfo.txt              |

Scenario: Add multiple environment details
	Users should be able to add multiple environment details via the Project Details page.

