	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment One |
	| Product            | Portal Production          |
	| Liferay Version    | 6.2 EE                     |
	| Operating System   | Windows Server 2012        |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 7               |
	| Application Server | Tomcat 7.0                 |
	| Database           | MariaDB 10.0               |
	| Cloud Services     | Azure SQL Databases        |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	| Portal EXT         | portal-ext.properties      |
	| Patch Info         | patchinfo.txt              |
	And the environment configuration with the name "Zen Portal Environment Two" should be visible with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment Two |
	| Product            | Portal Production          |
	| Liferay Version    | 6.1 GA3                    |
	| Operating System   | CentOS 6                   |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 6               |
	| Application Server | JBoss AS 7.1               |
	| Database           | SQL Server 2008            |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	| Portal EXT         | portal-ext.properties      |
	| Patch Info         | patchinfo.txt              |

Scenario: Edit environment details
	Users should be able to edit environment details via the Project Details page.

	Given I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I go to the project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I add an environment configuration with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment One |
	| Product            | Portal Production          |
	| Liferay Version    | 6.2 EE                     |
	| Operating System   | Windows Server 2012        |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 7               |
	| Application Server | Tomcat 7.0                 |
	| Database           | MariaDB 10.0               |
	| Cloud Services     | Azure SQL Databases        |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	| Portal EXT         | portal-ext.properties      |
	| Patch Info         | patchinfo.txt              |
	And I edit the environment configuration with the name "Zen Portal Environment One" with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment Two |
	| Product            | Portal Production          |
	| Liferay Version    | 6.1 GA3                    |
	| Operating System   | CentOS 6                   |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 6               |
	| Application Server | JBoss AS 7.1               |
	| Database           | SQL Server 2008            |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	Then the environment configuration with the name "Zen Portal Environment Two" should be visible with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment Two |
	| Product            | Portal Production          |
	| Liferay Version    | 6.1 GA3                    |
	| Operating System   | CentOS 6                   |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 6               |
	| Application Server | JBoss AS 7.1               |
	| Database           | SQL Server 2008            |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	| Portal EXT         | portal-ext.properties      |
	| Patch Info         | patchinfo.txt              |
	And the environment configuration with the name "Zen Portal Environment One" should not be visible

Scenario: Delete environment details
	Users should be able to delete environment details via the Project Details page.

	Given I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I go to the project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I add an environment configuration with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment One |
	| Product            | Portal Production          |
	| Liferay Version    | 6.2 EE                     |
	| Operating System   | Windows Server 2012        |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 7               |
	| Application Server | Tomcat 7.0                 |
	| Database           | MariaDB 10.0               |
	| Cloud Services     | Azure SQL Databases        |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	| Portal EXT         | portal-ext.properties      |
	| Patch Info         | patchinfo.txt              |
	And I delete the environment configuration with the name "Zen Portal Environment One"
	Then the environment configuration with the name "Zen Portal Environment One" should not be visible

Scenario: Add support instructions
	Users should be able to add support instructions via the Project Details page.

	Given I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I go to the project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I add support instructions with the content "Support Instructions Content"
	Then the support instructions with the content "Support Instructions Content" should be visible

Scenario: Edit support instructions
	Users should be able to edit support instructions via the Project Details page.

	Given I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I go to the project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And I add support instructions with the content "Support Instructions Content"
	And I edit support instructions with the content " Edit"
	Then the support instructions with the content "Support Instructions Content Edit" should be visible

Scenario: View project offerings as customer and partner
	Projects created in OSB should have certain elements visible to customers and partners in the project details page.

	Given I edit a project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive" and code "ZENOSBA" to have a support lifetime of "1 Minute" starting "60" days ago for the product "Portal Production"
	And I automatically have all expired projects moved to on hold status
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I go to the Offerings tab
	Then the offering with the product name "Portal Production" should not be visible
	And the offering with the product name "Digital Enterprise Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Digital Enterprise Production |
	| SLA              | Platinum                      |
	| Start Date       | Today                         |
	| Support End Date | 1 year from now               |
	| Licenses         | 0 / 1                         |
	| Tickets          | Unlimited                     |
	| Version          | 7                             |
	| Instance Size    | Sizing 1                      |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                        |
	And the offering with the product name "Liferay Commerce Connectors Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Liferay Commerce Connectors Production |
	| SLA              | Floating                               |
	| Start Date       | Today                                  |
	| Support End Date | 1 year from now                        |
	| Licenses         | 0 / 0                                  |
	| Tickets          | 0                                      |
	| Instance Size    | Sizing 1                               |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                                 |
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I go to the Offerings tab
	Then the offering with the product name "Portal Production" should not be visible
	And the offering with the product name "Digital Enterprise Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Digital Enterprise Production |
	| SLA              | Platinum                      |
	| Start Date       | Today                         |
	| Support End Date | 1 year from now               |
	| Licenses         | 0 / 1                         |
	| Tickets          | Unlimited                     |
	| Version          | 7                             |
	| Instance Size    | Sizing 1                      |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                        |
	And the offering with the product name "Liferay Commerce Connectors Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Liferay Commerce Connectors Production |
	| SLA              | Floating                               |
	| Start Date       | Today                                  |
	| Support End Date | 1 year from now                        |
	| Licenses         | 0 / 0                                  |
	| Tickets          | 0                                      |
	| Instance Size    | Sizing 1                               |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                                 |
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I go to the Offerings tab
	Then the offering with the product name "Portal Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Portal Production |
	| SLA              | Gold              |
